00:57:37.440 --> 00:57:40.210
- Well, the first thing
I'll say is that another way

00:57:40.210 --> 00:57:42.940
of thinking about the Green
New Deal framework is standards

00:57:42.940 --> 00:57:44.190
investment justice.

00:57:44.190 --> 00:57:46.760
And so standards are not outside

00:57:46.760 --> 00:57:49.100
of the purview of a
Green New Deal framework.

00:57:49.100 --> 00:57:51.480
And a lot of the ways that people tend

00:57:51.480 --> 00:57:54.890
to think about what's outside
are more like cap and trade

00:57:54.890 --> 00:57:57.650
carbon pricing sort of
market-based mechanisms

00:57:57.650 --> 00:57:59.680
to environmental policy.

00:57:59.680 --> 00:58:03.430
The reason why we can't just
do an investment only approach

00:58:03.430 --> 00:58:05.210
is because we will not get where we need

00:58:05.210 --> 00:58:07.750
to go at the pace and
scale that's necessary.

00:58:07.750 --> 00:58:10.840
What all the modeling shows
is that you give money

00:58:10.840 --> 00:58:14.910
but it doesn't get you to
the deployment that you need.

00:58:14.910 --> 00:58:16.520
And so we have to have some kind

00:58:16.520 --> 00:58:19.640
of requirement to mop
up at the end of the day

00:58:19.640 --> 00:58:22.040
and say it's great that
you're building stuff

00:58:22.040 --> 00:58:24.900
but you actually need
to build enough stuff.

00:58:24.900 --> 00:58:27.880
And then with climate change,
there's a huge difference.

00:58:27.880 --> 00:58:30.270
And I think this is one of
the fundamental contributions

00:58:30.270 --> 00:58:33.460
of the Green New Deal
thinking about the scale

00:58:33.460 --> 00:58:34.870
and the scope of the problem

00:58:34.870 --> 00:58:37.990
the pace that's necessary,
not just sort of saying,

00:58:37.990 --> 00:58:39.470
oh we'll do a little climate policy.

00:58:39.470 --> 00:58:40.730
We'll, put a price on carbon,

00:58:40.730 --> 00:58:42.680
hope that it reduces some emissions.

00:58:42.680 --> 00:58:45.090
We actually say here's how much
emissions we have to reduce.

00:58:45.090 --> 00:58:46.690
Here's how much clean power we need.

00:58:46.690 --> 00:58:47.990
Here's when we need it by.

00:58:47.990 --> 00:58:49.990
That was one of the key things

00:58:49.990 --> 00:58:52.990
in terms of reframing it
around 2030 in particular.

